{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1466890-n-we-unleashed","id":1466890,"title":"N!WE Unleashed!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-05T21:16:34-07:00","id":1466890,"title":"N!WE Unleashed!","content":"I just finished reading the PDF and submitting the errata I found. Overall a surprisingly good book. I didn't expect a wrestling book to be as interesting as it turned out to be.<br /> <br /> Good point: Their system for modeling wrestling matches seemed interesting.<br /> <br /> Bad point: Most of the nova wrestlers seemed to default to a few dots in Mega-Attributes and Mega Edges. Most even built their Signature Moves off the same two techniques. I'd have been more interested in example characters with flashier powers, like kinetic energy manipulation, Teleport, Quantum Agent, or Shrinking.<br /> <br /> Weird point: I think the strongest nova in the world is a wrestler. Duke &quot;Core&quot; Baron has Quantum 7, and between Mega-Might and Boost: Might, his effective Mega-Might climbs to somewhere between 5 and 7, depending on his base Attribute dots.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T03:18:26-07:00","id":1466922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1466890-n-we-unleashed#post1466890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just finished reading the PDF and submitting the errata I found. Overall a surprisingly good book. I didn't expect a wrestling book to be as interesting as it turned out to be.<br /> <br /> Good point: Their system for modeling wrestling matches seemed interesting.<br /> <br /> Bad point: Most of the nova wrestlers seemed to default to a few dots in Mega-Attributes and Mega Edges. Most even built their Signature Moves off the same two techniques. I'd have been more interested in example characters with flashier powers, like kinetic energy manipulation, Teleport, Quantum Agent, or Shrinking.<br /> <br /> Weird point: I think the strongest nova in the world is a wrestler. Duke &amp;quot;Core&amp;quot; Baron has Quantum 7, and between Mega-Might and Boost: Might, his effective Mega-Might climbs to somewhere between 5 and 7, depending on his base Attribute dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any interesting plot hooks?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T04:15:59-07:00","id":1466924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1466890-n-we-unleashed?p=1466922#post1466922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any interesting plot hooks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Many! There is a big list of wrestlers in the end with so many hooks you can build any kind of game around. Novas trying to become real crime fighters, wrestlers that are egomaniac, violent or any weird in a general way that can become focus of the police (or nova groups), drug abuse and addiction, etc, the list is quite long.<br /> <br /> I really love the system for the wrestling mini game, you can use it in many ways, basically any kind of competition with somewhat restrict rules, like basketball or competitive martial arts that don\u2019t go until knock out, etc, can use an variation of the rules with little changes (most in the fluffy), in a way it would not be a sequence of rolls with no change and no interference from the others, like regular competitions would be (the first to get X successes wins).<br /> <br /> The game rolls around basically human wrestling, with Novas fighting mostly as humans with their powers working in cosmetic ways, and occasionally giving scale in certain situations, so there are a list of moves (that are not long, but cover basically all the possible results in the mini game) and a list of Nova moves that are more powerful, but require more successes in the roll, what regular humans would not reach regularly, so Novas can do more stuff, but they are not winning automatically. Also it considers that the winner of the minigame can be different from the winner of the fight, you can say the other guy won (as it was defined by the producers), but the victory didn\u2019t get the eyes of the public, while the fight looser end up more popular (winning the mini game).<br /> <br /> Its not about real fights, it\u2019s about professional wrestling and all that we know about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T08:14:58-07:00","id":1466947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1466890-n-we-unleashed?p=1466922#post1466922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any interesting plot hooks?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a persistent condition called &quot;Becoming the Mask&quot; that can leave high Flux novas convinced they're their in ring characters, which can be quite dangerous depending on the character. OTOH the condition currently has some problems with the mechanics, which I noted in an errata submission. It is specifically a result of generating too much Flux in the ring, but the book's stripped down rules for fights in the ring provide no method for gaining Flux.<br /> <br /> There are also plot hooks regarding drug addiction, mysterious deaths, shadowy cabals of backers, a missing mentor, and a fighter whose powers are starting to go out of control.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T17:29:36-07:00","id":1467000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1466890-n-we-unleashed?p=1466947#post1466947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a persistent condition called &amp;quot;Becoming the Mask&amp;quot; that can leave high Flux novas convinced they're their in ring characters, which can be quite dangerous depending on the character. OTOH the condition currently has some problems with the mechanics, which I noted in an errata submission. It is specifically a result of generating too much Flux in the ring, but the book's stripped down rules for fights in the ring provide no method for gaining Flux.<br /> <br /> There are also plot hooks regarding drug addiction, mysterious deaths, shadowy cabals of backers, a missing mentor, and a fighter whose powers are starting to go out of control.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. Also, I totally agree with your analysis of Divis Mal in the other thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T17:27:09-08:00","id":1467132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1466890-n-we-unleashed#post1466890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bad point: Most of the nova wrestlers seemed to default to a few dots in Mega-Attributes and Mega Edges. Most even built their Signature Moves off the same two techniques. I'd have been more interested in example characters with flashier powers, like kinetic energy manipulation, Teleport, Quantum Agent, or Shrinking.<br /> <br /> Weird point: I think the strongest nova in the world is a wrestler. Duke &quot;Core&quot; Baron has Quantum 7, and between Mega-Might and Boost: Might, his effective Mega-Might climbs to somewhere between 5 and 7, depending on his base Attribute dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also kind of weird - which I put in feedback after commenting on it over on the Discord and IanW suggesting I do so - that none of the example novas seem to go in for nonstandard body plans. Maybe it's just my players, but I always seem to have at least one nova who has wings, or different-colored skin, or whatnot. Closest you get is Superbeast who transforms in the ring but is just a basic hot rocker guy outside of it.<br /> <br /> It's not the sort of thing that makes me massively disappointed in the book by any means, since it's the sort of thing you could easily explain in character (N!WE doesn't want to hire weird-looking people!) but it felt like a missed opportunity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T18:06:11-08:00","id":1467210,"title":"","content":"There is sort of a precedent, with <i>many</i> people over the years noting on Vince McMahon's seeming obsession with performers of a certain body type (especially height and physique) and apparent inability to understand (or believe) how ones who don't fit that mold are able to get over with fans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T15:50:50-08:00","id":1471806,"title":"","content":"I downloaded the revised version of the book. Looks fairly good, and they caught most of the errata I sent in. The biggest issues I can still see offhand:<br /> 1). The front and back covers have disappeared from the PDF. Hope they fix that before people start getting them PoD.<br /> 2). Most of the Paths now have over 15 dots in Edges, which is at least better than coming in with too few dots.<br /> 3). In attempting to fix the Sports Reporter Path, they wound up with: &quot;<span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Big HeaFame,</span></span>&quot;. Not sure how that got through spellcheck.<br /> 4). Both the &quot;Becoming the Mask&quot; condition and the &quot;Mask&quot; Persona Edge involve Flux gained during matches, but the Squared Circle rules provide no mechanics for gaining Flux during a match.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","user":"Shepherdboi","date":". 01-04-2022, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}